# Generated by scripts/build_lexicon.py from hachidaishu-utf8-1.0.db
# (all 8 anthologies). See that script's module docstring for the
# POS-tagging pipeline (real yamagen/hachidaishu algorithm, not a
# hand-transcribed static table) and known simplifications.
#
# URI convention (as of 2026-08-11, a further split on top of
# 2026-08-10's reading-keyed design -- see design-notes.md's sense
# entries for both dates): ontolex:LexicalEntry is keyed by
# reading + bg_group (bg_id truncated to prefix-AA-BB, see
# bg_group()), so different kanji spellings sharing one reading
# still merge into one entry (e.g. 写る/映る/移る, all うつる) but
# only within the same rough WLSP classification -- senses that
# are really different words sharing a reading (e.g. たつ's
# 建つ/断つ・絶つ・立つ・裁つ/竜・辰, five different entries) land in
# separate entries instead of one entry swallowing every sense
# regardless of meaning. The URI local name itself is
# "読み【字型1・字型2】" (entry_display_name()) -- kanji forms
# deduped, drawn only from this entry's own post-split sense group,
# no bg_id visible in the name. Two different bg_groups under one
# reading occasionally produce the identical kanji-set (single-kanji
# polysemy, e.g. あさ's 麻 in two unrelated WLSP categories) --
# those collide onto the same URI on purpose (no bg_id suffix, per
# the user 2026-08-11) and their properties simply accumulate on
# the shared subject, an accepted residual merge, not a bug.
# ontolex:LexicalSense stays kanji+bg_id-keyed
# (lex:立つ-BG-02-1513-01-0100) -- unaffected, still full bg_id,
# still truncated to AA-BBBB for ontolex:reference. An entry's
# ontolex:canonicalForm lists the reading plus every attested kanji
# spelling (within its own split group) as separate writtenRep
# values. A reading used only by function-word occurrences gets a
# "*"-suffixed reading (lex:な\*【…】) so it doesn't merge with an
# unrelated content-word entry sharing the same bare reading
# (lex:な【…】) -- see entry_key().

